---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/licenses.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="wArcxs Licenses — hosted licensing for Minecraft clients and tools" description="wArcxs Licenses: hosted access control for client builds. Signed validation, tiers, feature flags and machine limits from a panel and Discord bot.">
  <div class="lz">
    <header class="lz-nav">
      <div class="lz-nav-in">
        <a class="lz-mark" href="/products/licenses">wArcxs <span>Licenses</span></a>
        <ul class="lz-side">
          <li><a href="#features">features</a></li>
          <li><a href="#code">code</a></li>
          <li><a href="#pricing">pricing</a></li>
          <li><a href="/products/licenses/docs">docs</a></li>
          <li><a href="/products/licenses/login">sign in</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="lz-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Give every build a key.<br><em>Keep the control.</em></h1>
        <p>A hosted license system for Minecraft clients, launchers and tools. Generate keys, control machine access, gate modules or build channels by tier, and revoke leaked access from one panel or Discord bot.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href="#pricing">See pricing</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/products/licenses/docs">Read the docs</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="verdict" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="v-top"><span class="v-dot"></span> validate · <em>signed</em></div>
        <div class="v-key">wArcxs-7QX4-9F2K-M8A2</div>
        <dl class="v-rows">
          <div><dt>product</dt><dd>MY_APP</dd></div>
          <div><dt>tier</dt><dd class="acc">PREMIUM</dd></div>
          <div><dt>servers</dt><dd>2 / 3 in use</dd></div>
          <div><dt>signature</dt><dd class="ok">✓ verified</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-line">
      <h2>One system for the <em>whole life</em> of a build.</h2>
      <p>Issue keys, bind them to the machines you allow, verify every client launch, unlock modules or channels by tier, and revoke leaked access — all from one panel and a Discord bot. We host the validation layer; you integrate once.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-use">
      <div class="lz-uhead">
        <h2>Built for the client software <em>you actually ship</em>.</h2>
        <p>If it can make an HTTPS request, it can validate access. Typical client-side use cases:</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ugrid">
        <div class="ucard">
          <h3>Minecraft clients &amp; plugins</h3>
          <p>Distribute from your site or Discord, bind access to the buyer you issued it to, let users retrieve keys with <span class="mono">/mylicenses</span>, and revoke leaked access without rebuilding the client.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ucard">
          <h3>Launchers &amp; desktop tools</h3>
          <p>A launcher, Java client or desktop utility running on the user's machine. Fingerprint the device, cap allowed seats and expose modules or build channels by tier without hosting your own license server.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ucard">
          <h3>SaaS backends &amp; APIs</h3>
          <p>Gate your own service by plan. Read <span class="mono">featureFlags</span> on each request to flip export, API access or seat counts on and off, and move a customer between tiers without shipping a deploy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ucard">
          <h3>Indie software &amp; scripts</h3>
          <p>Selling from your own site or Gumroad? Drop in a few lines, embed one public key, and every copy checks in — perpetual or subscription, whichever you sell.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-hosted">
      <div class="lz-hosted-card">
        <h2>We run it. <em>You ship the builds.</em></h2>
        <p>The validation endpoint, panel and Discord bot run on our infrastructure — <strong>nothing extra to deploy and no license database for you to maintain.</strong> You issue access and ship builds; keeping validation online is our problem, not yours.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-rows" id="features">
      <article class="frow">
        <div class="frow-text">
          <h3>Locked to the machines <em>you allow</em>.</h3>
          <p>Sell one seat and it stays one seat. Cap a key to a set number of machines with an IP limit on each, tied to a device fingerprint you compute. Spin it up on a box you didn't authorise and the check comes back <span class="mono">SERVER_CAP_EXCEEDED</span> — no shared key quietly running across a whole network.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="frow-vis">
          <div class="v-servers">
            <div class="vs-cap">cap · 3 servers · 2 IPs each</div>
            <ul>
              <li class="ok"><span class="s">london-01</span><span class="t">✓ active</span></li>
              <li class="ok"><span class="s">frankfurt-02</span><span class="t">✓ active</span></li>
              <li class="no"><span class="s">unknown-03</span><span class="t">✗ over cap</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="frow rev">
        <div class="frow-vis">
          <div class="v-sign">
            <div class="vsg-h">response · signed</div>
            <code>valid: true · tier: PREMIUM</code>
            <div class="v-sig"><span class="lbl">X-Signature</span><span class="ok">✓ verified</span></div>
            <div class="v-sig-sub">edit the reply in transit → the signature breaks</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="frow-text">
          <h3>A verdict nobody can <em>forge</em>.</h3>
          <p>Cracking a license usually means patching the “yes” into the response. Here every answer is signed with your tenant's private key and verified against a public key baked into your build. Intercept the traffic, flip <span class="mono">valid</span> to true, and the signature stops matching — so your app throws it out. The answer is only ever as good as its signature.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="frow">
        <div class="frow-text">
          <h3>Gate modules. <em>Revoke leaks.</em></h3>
          <p>Ship one client and decide what each user gets at validation time. Tiers and feature flags can expose specific modules, configs or build channels without a re-release. If a key leaks, revoke the key, machine or account and the next validation is denied.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="frow-vis">
          <div class="v-tiers">
            <span class="stamp">revocable</span>
            <div class="vt-head"><span class="lbl">tier</span><b>PREMIUM</b></div>
            <ul class="vt-flags">
              <li class="on"><span class="fn">export</span><span class="t">✓ unlocked</span></li>
              <li class="on"><span class="fn">api access</span><span class="t">✓ unlocked</span></li>
              <li class="off"><span class="fn">white-label</span><span class="t">✕ locked</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-more">
      <div class="lz-mhead"><h2>More <em>in the box</em>.</h2></div>
      <div class="mgrid">
        <div class="mcard">
          <h3>Subscriptions or perpetual</h3>
          <p>Sell both from the same system. Time-box a key and the day it lapses it validates as <span class="mono">EXPIRED</span>; renewals just push the date forward — no new build, no re-ship.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcard">
          <h3>Self-serve <span class="mono">/mylicenses</span></h3>
          <p>Buyers look up, transfer and reset their own keys from the panel or straight from Discord. You stop being the help desk for every lost or misplaced key.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcard">
          <h3>Replay-proof &amp; rate-limited</h3>
          <p>Every request carries a one-time <span class="mono">nonce</span> and a timestamp. Record a valid response and fire it forever? It's rejected as <span class="mono">NONCE_REPLAY</span>, and abusive callers get throttled.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-code" id="code">
      <div class="lz-chead">
        <h2>A few lines, <em>in any language</em>.</h2>
        <p>On the JVM, drop in the zero-dependency SDK — it makes the call and checks the signature for you. Anywhere else, hit the same documented endpoint with your standard library: send the key, verify the signature, act on the verdict. That's the whole integration.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lzc">
        <div class="lzc-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Language">
          <button type="button" class="lzc-tab on" data-tab="java" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Java · SDK</button>
          <button type="button" class="lzc-tab" data-tab="node" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Node.js · HTTP</button>
          <button type="button" class="lzc-tab" data-tab="python" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Python · HTTP</button>
        </div>
        <pre class="lzc-code lzc-panel on" data-panel="java"><code><span class="row"><span class="gut">01</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-type">LicenseResult</span> <span class="hljs-variable">r</span> <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> client.validate(key, ServerFingerprint.derive());</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">02</span><span class="src"> </span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">03</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (!r.valid())                       <span class="hljs-comment">// false unless the signature verified too</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">04</span><span class="src">    <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> lockOut(r.reason());</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">05</span><span class="src"> </span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">06</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (<span class="hljs-string">&quot;PREMIUM&quot;</span>.equals(r.tier()))</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">07</span><span class="src">    enablePremiumFeatures();</span></span></code></pre>
        <pre class="lzc-code lzc-panel" data-panel="node"><code><span class="row"><span class="gut">01</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> res = <span class="hljs-keyword">await</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">fetch</span>(url, &#123;</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">02</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">method</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;POST&quot;</span>,</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">03</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">headers</span>: &#123; <span class="hljs-string">&quot;Content-Type&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;application/json&quot;</span> &#125;,</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">04</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">body</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">JSON</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">stringify</span>(&#123; <span class="hljs-attr">licenseKey</span>: key, <span class="hljs-attr">productCode</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;MY_APP&quot;</span>,</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">05</span><span class="src">    serverId, <span class="hljs-attr">nonce</span>: crypto.<span class="hljs-title function_">randomUUID</span>(), <span class="hljs-attr">timestamp</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Date</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">now</span>() &#125;),</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">06</span><span class="src">&#125;);</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">07</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> body = <span class="hljs-title class_">Buffer</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">from</span>(<span class="hljs-keyword">await</span> res.<span class="hljs-title function_">arrayBuffer</span>());   <span class="hljs-comment">// exact bytes</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">08</span><span class="src"> </span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">09</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> ok = crypto.<span class="hljs-title function_">createVerify</span>(<span class="hljs-string">&quot;RSA-SHA256&quot;</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">update</span>(body)</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">10</span><span class="src">  .<span class="hljs-title function_">verify</span>(<span class="hljs-variable constant_">PUBLIC_KEY_PEM</span>, res.<span class="hljs-property">headers</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">get</span>(<span class="hljs-string">&quot;X-Signature&quot;</span>), <span class="hljs-string">&quot;base64&quot;</span>);</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">11</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (!ok || !<span class="hljs-title class_">JSON</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">parse</span>(body).<span class="hljs-property">valid</span>) <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">lockOut</span>();</span></span></code></pre>
        <pre class="lzc-code lzc-panel" data-panel="python"><code><span class="row"><span class="gut">01</span><span class="src">res = urlopen(Request(url, json.dumps(&#123;</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">02</span><span class="src">    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;licenseKey&quot;</span>: key, <span class="hljs-string">&quot;productCode&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;MY_APP&quot;</span>, <span class="hljs-string">&quot;serverId&quot;</span>: server_id,</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">03</span><span class="src">    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;nonce&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">str</span>(uuid4()), <span class="hljs-string">&quot;timestamp&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">int</span>(time() * <span class="hljs-number">1000</span>),</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">04</span><span class="src">&#125;).encode(), &#123;<span class="hljs-string">&quot;Content-Type&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;application/json&quot;</span>&#125;))</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">05</span><span class="src">raw, sig = res.read(), res.headers[<span class="hljs-string">&quot;X-Signature&quot;</span>]   <span class="hljs-comment"># exact bytes</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">06</span><span class="src"> </span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">07</span><span class="src">pub.verify(b64decode(sig), raw, padding.PKCS1v15(), SHA256())</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">08</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">not</span> json.loads(raw)[<span class="hljs-string">&quot;valid&quot;</span>]:</span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">09</span><span class="src">    lock_out()</span></span></code></pre>
        <p class="lzc-cap">Java drops in the zero-dependency SDK — it makes the call and verifies the signature for you. Any other language calls the same endpoint and verifies the response itself.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lzc lzc-resp">
        <div class="lzc-tabs static"><span class="lzc-restag">↳ the signed answer</span></div>
        <pre class="lzc-code"><code><span class="row"><span class="gut">01</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-punctuation">&#123;</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">02</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;valid&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-literal"><span class="hljs-keyword">true</span></span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">03</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;tier&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-string">&quot;PREMIUM&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">04</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;expiresAt&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-string">&quot;2027-01-01T00:00:00Z&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">05</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;featureFlags&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-punctuation">&#123;</span> <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;export&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-literal"><span class="hljs-keyword">true</span></span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span> <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;api&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-literal"><span class="hljs-keyword">true</span></span> <span class="hljs-punctuation">&#125;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">06</span><span class="src">  <span class="hljs-attr">&quot;nonce&quot;</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-string">&quot;3f2a9c1e-...&quot;</span></span></span><span class="row"><span class="gut">07</span><span class="src"><span class="hljs-punctuation">&#125;</span></span></span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lz-pricing" id="pricing">
      <div class="lz-phead">
        <h2>Every plan includes <em>the full access layer</em>.</h2>
        <p>Signed validation, machine limits, tiers, revocation, the panel and the bot are included on every plan. You only scale by how many keys and client products you need.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ptable">
        <div class="pcol">
          <div class="phd">
            <span class="pname">Basic</span>
            <span class="ptagline">A solid start for a small release.</span>
          </div>
          <span class="pprice"><span class="pcur">€</span>9<span class="pper">/mo</span></span>
          <ul class="plims">
            <li><b>250</b> licenses</li>
            <li><b>1</b> product</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn ghost pbtn" href="/products/licenses/login">Get started</a>
        </div>
        <div class="pcol on">
          <span class="ptag">most&nbsp;chosen</span>
          <div class="phd">
            <span class="pname">Pro</span>
            <span class="ptagline">For active projects with a real customer base.</span>
          </div>
          <span class="pprice"><span class="pcur">€</span>19<span class="pper">/mo</span></span>
          <ul class="plims">
            <li><b>1,500</b> licenses</li>
            <li><b>5</b> products</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn primary pbtn" href="/products/licenses/login">Get started</a>
        </div>
        <div class="pcol">
          <div class="phd">
            <span class="pname">Enterprise</span>
            <span class="ptagline">For teams, resellers and larger deployments.</span>
          </div>
          <span class="pprice"><span class="pcur">€</span>49<span class="pper">/mo+</span></span>
          <ul class="plims">
            <li><b>5,000+</b> licenses</li>
            <li><b>Unlimited</b> products</li>
            <li>Priority support &amp; custom terms</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn ghost pbtn" href="mailto:hello@warcxs.com">Talk to us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="lz-foot">
      <span>2026 wArcxs Licenses &mdash; &copy; All rights reserved</span>
      <nav><a href="/products/licenses/docs">Docs</a><a href="https://warcxs.com/discord" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Community</a><a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a><a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy</a></nav>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script type="module">
    function initLicenses() {
      document.querySelectorAll('.lz-code .lzc').forEach(container => {
        if (container.dataset.tabbound) return;
        let tabs = container.querySelectorAll('.lzc-tab');
        if (tabs.length) {
          container.dataset.tabbound = '1';
          tabs.forEach(tab => {
            tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
              let panelName = tab.dataset.tab;
              tabs.forEach(t => {
                let selected = t === tab;
                t.classList.toggle('on', selected);
                t.setAttribute('aria-selected', selected ? 'true' : 'false');
              });
              container.querySelectorAll('.lzc-panel').forEach(p => {
                p.classList.toggle('on', p.dataset.panel === panelName);
              });
            });
          });
        }
      });
    }
    initLicenses();
    document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initLicenses);
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
